1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,800
I'm not a programmer. For about two years I've been learning to work together with AI.

2
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:12,300
What annoyed me most was that I gave an agent a mission from A to Z,

3
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:16,600
and it did a piece, suddenly stopped, and afterwards I didn't know

4
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:21,000
what was done, what wasn't, and why everything was standing still.

5
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:27,600
I already have so many of these AI projects that sometimes I can't keep track of all of it myself.

6
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:35,400
That's why I wanted to create something that would show the truth about the agents' work,

7
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:41,000
and not just their assurances that everything is ready.

8
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:54,000
I want a tool that can show the truth about agents' work, help recover an interrupted mission

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,500
and bring it to a confirmed completion.

10
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:14,500
Mission from A to Z: green only with proof.

11
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:38,500
I would like other people to be able to use it too, because I'm surely not the only one with this problem.

12
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:58,000
I can't write this kind of code myself, but I have ideas, I plan with agents

13
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:05,500
and I try to understand better and better how to use their capabilities.

14
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:18,300
And that's exactly what excites me most: that a person without a programming education

15
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:23,000
can have an idea and, together with AI, make a tool that really works.

16
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:29,500
Pretty promises don't matter to me. What matters to me is real action and an honest showing of our work.
